WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.390
There are plenty of great underappreciated
movie trilogies to dive into, whether they're

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.040
small indies or movies you love but didn't
realize were part of a trilogy.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.400
For your next lazy Sunday, settle in, pull
up your favorite streaming service, and fall

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.580
in love with a new three-part film series.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.960
Directed by Richard Linklater, this trilogy
spans continents, decades, and takes a deep

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.880
look at the changing nature of long-time relationships.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:28.040
Before Sunrise finds Jesse and Céline locking
eyes on a train and experiencing one long

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.280
night in Vienna filled with revelations, deep
connections, and love at first sight.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.180
The second film, Before Sunset, focuses on
the compromises and changes you make in your

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.480
thirties as Jesse and Céline reconnect after
nine years apart.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.500
"Each relationship, when it ends, really damages
me.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.380
I never fully recover.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.560
That's why I'm very careful of getting involved,
because it hurts too much."

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.560
Before Midnight jumps ahead another nine years
after that.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.320
Through Jesse and Céline's long and passionate
love story, nearly every viewer will be able

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.120
to find at least one striking similarity to
their own life.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:06.200
El Mariachi follows an out-of-work musician
simply known as El Mariachi, who is mistaken

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.600
for a ruthless criminal by a murderous gang.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.380
Unbeknownst to many fans, it's also the first
film of a trilogy that includes the far more

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.420
popular Desperado and Once Upon a Time in
Mexico.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.940
Part of that confusion comes down to recasting;
Carlos Gallardo played El Mariachi in the

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.180
first film, but he was replaced by Antonio
Banderas for the final two films.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.400
Together, the three films showcase all the
over-the-top violence and melodrama that any

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.480
Robert Rodriguez fan could ask for.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.600
Based on Stieg Larsson's series about a vengeful
young hacker named Lisbeth Salander, this

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:42.650
film franchise originally aired on Swedish
channel SVT1 as a miniseries, though each

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.840
installment totaled around three hours each.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.700
The first film, The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo,
introduces us to Salander, who is helping

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.600
disgraced journalist Mikael investigate a
missing person.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.520
Throughout the next two films, The Girl Who
Played with Fire and The Girl Who Kicked the

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.290
Hornet's Nest, Mikael and Salander continue
working together, and when Salander is wrongly

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:05.600
accused of murdering a journalist who was
targeting Mikael, he works to prove her innocence.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.319
The Hannibal Lecter trilogy features other
films and adaptations beyond these three films,

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.740
but these installments make up the core of
the franchise.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.880
Based on the series of novels by Thomas Harris,
the film adaptations begin with The Silence

00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:20.010
of the Lambs.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.579
Starring Jodie Foster as Clarice and Anthony
Hopkins as Hannibal Lecter, the story finds

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:28.829
its unlikely partners teaming up to track
down another sadistic serial killer known

00:02:28.829 --> 00:02:29.740
as Buffalo Bill.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:35.540
The film is inarguably a classic, winning
nearly half a dozen oscar awards in 1992,

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.040
with some of the most memorable dialogue in
film history

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.820
"A census taker once tried to test me.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.640
I ate his liver with some fava beans and a
nice chianti."

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.500
Hopkins reprised his role in Hannibal, but
Julianne Moore took over as Clarice.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.159
Red Dragon saw Hopkins return for a third
and final time, bringing all his considerable

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.320
charisma to the role of the cannibal doctor.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.820
There are technically six films in George
A. Romero's Night of the Living Dead film

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.320
series, but the first three are regarded as
their own independent trilogy.

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:11.060
Although the three originals don't share characters,
they all take place in the midst of a zombie

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.560
outbreak.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.889
1968's Night of the Living Dead focuses on
a group of seven people trapped in a remote

00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:19.960
Pennsylvania farmhouse which is surrounded
by living dead.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:24.160
It's a true horror classic, and one of the
most influential films ever made.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.120
Dawn of the Dead, released in 1978, was a
collaboration between Romero and Italian horror

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.939
filmmaker Dario Argento.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:37.280
Like its predecessor, it was filmed in Pennsylvania
on an incredibly low budget and was critically

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.329
adored, becoming one of the best known zombie
films of the 20th century.

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:46.859
Finally, Day of the Dead arrived in 1985,
telling the story of human survival in underground

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.460
cities and bunkers as the infestation continued.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.339
Each film in the trilogy left a lasting impact,
spawning countless remakes, parodies, and

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.580
homages for years to come.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.900
In 2004, director Edgar Wright, teamed up
with Simon Pegg and Nick Frost for Shaun of

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.960
the Dead, a wry, hilarious take on a typical
zombie flick.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.260
Next came their wonderfully absurd cop parody
Hot Fuzz in 2007.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.900
Finally, The World's End, their take on aliens
and the apocalypse, arrived in 2013, completing

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:23.840
the Cornetto trilogy.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:29.300
The trilogy's name comes from the famous British
frozen treat and each film features a different

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:34.210
color of Cornetto which relates to its plot:
red for Shaun of the Dead, blue for Hot Fuzz,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.260
and green for The World's End.

00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:39.840
Though none of the films share the same universe,
watching each of them back to back gives viewers

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.220
the chance to spot plenty of jokes and references.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.340
Never taken a shortcut before?"

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.140
What's the matter Danny?  never taken a shortcut before?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.640
"Oh no!"

